{"result":{"atchFileId":"FILE_900000000006617","bbsId":"BBSMSTR_000000000081","bbsIds":null,"frstRegisterId":"USRCNFRM_00000000000","frstRegisterPnttm":"2015-11-13","lastUpdusrId":"","lastUpdusrPnttm":"","ntceBgnde":"2015-12-30          ","ntceEndde":"9999-11-30          ","ntcrId":"","ntcrNm":"","nttCn":"<p>2012~2014년에 실시된 진도 명량대첩로 해역 수중발굴조사(1~3차)의 보고서입니다. 이 해역에서는 조사구역 전반에 걸쳐 다량의 도자기가 발굴되었습니다. 특히 고려 중기의 기린&middot;오리&middot;원앙 모양의 청자향로뚜껑, 청자병, 청자기와 등 고급청자들이 출수되었습니다. 보고서는 I. 머릿말 / II. 조사해역의 환경 / III. 조사장비 및 내용 / IV. 출수유물 / V. 출수유물분석 / VI. 고찰 / VII. 맺음말 등으로 구성하였습니다. *담당부서 : 수중발굴과</p>","nttCnEn":"<p>The area of the sea where the relics have been found underwater is located in Myeongnyangdaecheop-ro, Jindo-gun, South Jeolla Province, 4km southeast of Uldolmok Strait where the Battle of Myeongnyang took place during Imjin War and 500m northwest of Byeokpa Harbor where the Battle of Byeokpajin occurred. After a group of people who tried to smuggle out nine pieces, including a celadon pillow, they rubbed from this area were arrested, National Research Institute of Maritime Cultural Heritage urgently started to explore this area from September 2012 and carried out three rounds of underwater excavation. As a result, we have found about 650 pieces of relics including metal, wooden or stone-made pieces as well as a variety of ceramics. This is an interim report on the exploration and excavation carried out from 2012 to 2014. The operation of excavation in the waters of Myeongnyangdaecheop-ro is only 5 percent completed and will be continued. In particular, since various types of relics have been discovered over a wide area, precise soil removing probes will be conducted continuously.</p>","nttCn2":"","nttCn3":"","nttCn4":"","nttCn5":"124","nttCn6":"","nttCn7":"","categoryDetailCode":"ACARPT001","categoryDetailCode2":"","nttId":904,"nttNo":1,"nttSj":"진도 명량대첩로 해역 수중발굴조사 보고서 Ⅰ","nttSjEn":"Waters off the Jindo Underwater Excavation Ⅰ","parnts":"0","password":"","inqireCo":5491,"re